        <briefdescription>
<para>Define a <ref refid="structmux__state" kindref="compound">mux_state</ref> object by name from a <computeroutput>mux-state-names</computeroutput> entry. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Equivalent to <ref refid="group__mux__interface_1gac162201caf07686e7c9c8cd736ebf7e2" kindref="member">MUX_STATE_DT_SPEC_DEFINE_BY_IDX()</ref> with the index resolved from the <computeroutput>mux-state-names</computeroutput> property.</para>
<para>Example devicetree fragment: <verbatim>n: node {
        mux-states      = &lt;&amp;mux0 5 2&gt;, &lt;&amp;mux0 7 3&gt;;
        mux-state-names = &quot;default&quot;, &quot;alt&quot;;
};
</verbatim></para>
<para>Example usage: <verbatim>MUX_STATE_DT_SPEC_DEFINE_BY_NAME(DT_NODELABEL(n), default);
const struct mux_state *def =
        MUX_STATE_DT_GET_BY_NAME(DT_NODELABEL(n), default);
</verbatim></para>
