    <briefdescription>
<para>MUX Controller Interface. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Generic device model for multiplexer (signal-routing) controllers. The devicetree model is derived from Linux, but this subsystem intentionally does NOT provide shared-line arbitration: there is no mux_control_select()/deselect() and no per-control concurrency lock. A control line is assumed to have a single owner; concurrent consumers driving the same line are not protected against each other.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="since"><para>4.5 </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="version"><para>0.1.0 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
